    <ELEMENTS>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPDevelopmentErrorDetect</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00004</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Switches the development error detection and notification on or off. • true: detection and notification is enabled. • false: detection and notification is disabled.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 87 (printed page 87)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPDhcpOptionVinUse</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00067</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: If DoIPDhcpOptionVinUse is set to true the DoIP module will add the VIN to the Dhcp host name if no valid Dhcp host name is already set.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 87 (printed page 87)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPEntityStatusMaxByteFieldUse</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00064</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: This parameter is used to distinguish the optional support of the Max data size element of a diagnostic entity status response.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 87 (printed page 87)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPGIDInvalidityPattern</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00065</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 255</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Specifies the Byte pattern that is used for response messages if no valid GID could be retrieved. Only the value ’0’ or ’255’ is allowed".</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 88 (printed page 88)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPHostNameSizeMax</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00073</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 5 .. 255</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Maximum Size of the DHCP HostName in ASCII. This parameter is necessary to reserve the correct amount of bytes for working with the DHCP HostName option. Minimum range is 5 because Dhcp Host Name should be at least "DoIP-" on any configuration.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 88 (printed page 88)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPMainFunctionPeriod</L-4>
        </LABELS>
