      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPUseEIDasGID</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00018</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Specifies if the DoIP entity shall use its EID if it is the Master for vehicle identification gid on the vehicle identification/vehicle announcement.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 90 (printed page 90)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPVersionInfoApi</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00005</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Activates the DoIP_GetVersionInfo() API. TRUE: Enables the DoIP_GetVersionInfo() API. FALSE: DoIP_GetVersionInfo() API is not included.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 90 (printed page 90)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPVinGidMaster</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00017</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucBooleanParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Specifies if the DoIP entity is the Vehicle identification Master for the GID (Group ID).</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 90 (printed page 90)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPVinInvalidityPattern</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00066</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGeneral</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 255</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Specifies the Byte pattern that is used for response messages if no valid VIN could be retrieved. Only the value ’0’ or ’255’ is allowed".</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.3 DoIPGeneral; PDF page 91 (printed page 91)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPFurtherActionByteDirect</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00093</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPFurtherActionByteCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Description: Direct C Callback function to get the OEM specific Further Action Byte for the DoIP vehicle identification response/vehicle announcement. If the DoIPFurtherActionByteDirect parameter is present, the DoIP module will not use an RPort of ServiceInterface "CBGetFurtherActionByte" but will call the configured function.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.4 DoIPFurtherActionByteCallback; PDF page 94 (printed page 94)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPGetGidDirect</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00028</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPGetGidCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: If the DoIPGetGidDirect parameter exist the DoIP module shall call the configured callback function (&lt;User&gt;_DoIPGetGID) direct. (It is not needed to specify a service port to the DoIP service component.) If the DoIPGetGidDirect parameter does NOT exist the DoIP module shall use a RPort with a CallbackGetGID type of client-server port interface to retrive the GID.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.5 DoIPGetGidCallback; PDF page 95 (printed page 95)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPPowerModeDirect</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00027</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPPowerModeCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: If the DoIPPowerModeDirect parameter exist the DoIP module shall call the configured callback function (&lt;User&gt;_DoIPGetPowerModeCallback) direct. (It is not needed to specify a service port to the DoIP service component.) If the DoIPPowerModeDirect parameter does NOT present the DoIP module shall use a RPort with a CallbackGetPowerMode type of client-server port interface to retrive the current power mode.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.6 DoIPPowerModeCallback; PDF page 96 (printed page 96)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPTriggerGidSyncDirect</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00029</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPTriggerGidSyncCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: If the DoIPTriggerGidSyncDirect parameter exist the DoIP module shall call the configured callback function (&lt;User&gt;_DoIPTriggerGidSyncCallback) direct. (It is not needed to specify a service port to the DoIP service component.) If the DoIPTriggerGidSyncDirect parameter does NOT present the DoIP module shall use a RPort with a CallbackTriggerGIDSynchnonization type of client-server port interface to trigger the GID synchronization.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.7 DoIPTriggerGidSyncCallback; PDF page 96 (printed page 96)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPEid</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00014</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPConfigSet</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 281474976710655</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: 97 of 126 Document ID 418: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: true</P>
          <P>Description: Configured EID (Entity ID of) for vehicle identification/vehicle announcement. Only necessary if DoIPUseMacAddressForIdentification is set to FALSE.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.8 DoIPConfigSet; PDF page 97 (printed page 97)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPGid</L-4>
        </LABELS>
