      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPLogicalAddress</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00020</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPConfigSet</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 65535</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant true</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: true</P>
          <P>Description: Describes the logical address of the DoIP entity, i.e. the LA that will route diagnostic requests to the Dcm of the DoIP entity.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.8 DoIPConfigSet; PDF page 98 (printed page 98)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPInterface</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00100</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPConfigSet</P>
          <P>Type: EcucParamConfContainerDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1..255</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: This container defines a logical IP interface and collects properties to configure this interface.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Contains DoIPInterface configuration parameters and the subcontainers DoIPChannel, DoIPConnections, DoIPFurtherActionByteCallback, DoIPRoutingActivation, and DoIPTester.</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.9 DoIPInterface; PDF pages 99–105 (printed pages 99–105)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPAliveCheckResponseTimeout</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00009</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPInterface</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFloatParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: [0 .. INF]</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Timeout in [s] for waiting for a response to an Alive Check request before the connection is considered to be disconnected. Represents parameter T_TCP_AliveCheck of ISO 13400-2:2012.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.9 DoIPInterface; PDF page 99 (printed page 99)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPGeneralInactivityTime</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00068</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPInterface</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFloatParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: ]0 .. INF[</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Timeout in [s] for maximum inactivity of a TCP socket connection before the DoIP module will close the according socket connection. Represents parameter T_TCP_General_Inactivity of ISO 13400-2:2012</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.9 DoIPInterface; PDF page 100 (printed page 100)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPInitialInactivityTime</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00010</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPInterface</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFloatParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: ]0 .. INF[</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Timeout in [s] used for initial inactivity of a connected TCP socket connection directly after socket connection. Represents parameter T_TCP_Initial_Inactivity of ISO 13400-2:2012</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.9 DoIPInterface; PDF page 100 (printed page 100)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPInitialVehicleAnnouncementTime</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00008</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPInterface</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFloatParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: [0 .. INF]</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Time to wait in [s] for sending first vehicle anouncement message after IP address assignment. Represents parameter A_DoIP_Announce_Wait of ISO 13400-2:2012</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
