      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00035</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivation</P>
          <P>Type: EcucParamConfContainerDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Description: Container describes the Callbackfunction to call on a Routing Activation Request for Authentication. If this container is configured but the DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationFunc parameter is not present, the DoIP module will use an RPort of ServiceInterface &lt;RoutingActivation&gt;_RoutingActivation with the name "CB&lt;RoutingActivation&gt;RoutingActivation". &lt;RoutingActivation&gt; is the ShortName of the DoIPRoutingActiviation container.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Contains DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationFunc, DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationReqLength, and DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationResLength.</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.24 DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback; PDF page 121 (printed page 121)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationFunc</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00039</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Direct C Callback function to trigger the authentication function for routing activation. If the DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationFunc parameter is present, the DoIP module will not use an RPort of ServiceInterface &lt;RoutingActivation&gt;_RoutingActivation but call the configured function.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.24 DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback; PDF page 121 (printed page 121)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationReqLength</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00040</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 4</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Describes the amount of bytes used to handle to the authentication function on routing activation. If 0 is configured as length the parameter AuthenticationReqData will not be handled to the API.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.24 DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback; PDF page 122 (printed page 122)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationResLength</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00041</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucIntegerParamDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: 0 .. 4</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Post-Build Variant false</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Describes the amount of bytes used to read by the authentication function on routing activation. If 0 is configured as length the parameter AuthenticationResData will not be fetched via the API.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.24 DoIPRoutingActivationAuthenticationCallback; PDF page 122 (printed page 122)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationCallback</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00061</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivation</P>
          <P>Type: EcucParamConfContainerDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Description: Container describes the Callbackfunction to call on a Routing Activation Request for Confirmation. If this container is configured but the DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationFunc parameter is not present the DoIP module will use an RPort of ServiceInterface &lt;RoutingActivation&gt;_RoutingActivation with the name "CB&lt;RoutingActivation&gt;RoutingActivation". &lt;RoutingActivation&gt; is the ShortName of the DoIPRoutingActiviation container.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Contains DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationFunc, DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationReqLength, and DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationResLength.</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.25 DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationCallback; PDF page 123 (printed page 123)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
      </ANNOTATION>
      <ANNOTATION>
        <LABELS>
          <L-4>DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationFunc</L-4>
        </LABELS>
        <ANNOTATION-TEXT>
          <P>Source: AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticOverIP.pdf</P>
          <P>ECUCItemID: ECUC_DoIP_00036</P>
          <P>ParentContainer: DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationCallback</P>
          <P>Type: EcucFunctionNameDef</P>
          <P>RangeOrReferenceTarget: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>Multiplicity: 0..1</P>
          <P>DefaultValue: Regular Expression</P>
          <P>PostBuildVariant: false</P>
          <P>Description: Direct C Callback function to trigger the confirmation function for routing activation. If the DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationFunc parameter is present the DoIP module will not use an RPort of ServiceInterface &lt;RoutingActivation&gt;_RoutingActivation but call the configured function.</P>
          <P>Relationship: Not specified in source</P>
          <P>EvidenceClassification: Explicit</P>
          <P>SourceReference: 10.2.25 DoIPRoutingActivationConfirmationCallback; PDF page 123 (printed page 123)</P>
        </ANNOTATION-TEXT>
